<title>USA: CBOE to list 57 LEAPS with Jan 2000 expiration.</title>
<headline>CBOE to list 57 LEAPS with Jan 2000 expiration.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange said Thursday it will list LEAPS (Long-term Equity Anticipation Securities) with January 2000 expirations on 57 stocks on May 19.</p>
<p>For these 57 option classes, the existing LEAPS with January 1998 expirations will convert to standard options on May 19, the exchange said.</p>
<p>The CBOE, which lists 120 equity LEAPS, said it will introduce January 2000 expirations for the balance of its equity LEAPS listings in June and July.  </p>
<p>Among the new options will be January 2000 LEAPS on shares of AT&amp;T Corp, America Online Inc, Chrysler Corp, Citicorp and Cisco Systems Inc.</p>
<p>Also included will be Eastman Kodak Co, Exxon Corp, International Business Machines Corp, Merck &amp; Co Inc, Micron Technology Inc, Sears, Roebuck and Co, Telebras and Xerox.</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
